  ## Reusable knowledge
  
  - At the audited point, `editorial` had one published `weekly` (`revue-du-03-07`, category `pro`, `body_mdx` length 
26402), while 14 static `src/content/articles/actualites/revue-*.mdx` files rendered as free `/article/{slug}` pages. 
All inspected revues had `<MobileOnly>`, clean `##`/`###` boundaries, and 5-10 subjects, so splitting from stored MDX 
was feasible. [Task 1]
  ## Failures and how to do differently
  
> - Symptom: migration planning assumes roughly 20 weekly revues in the database. Cause: the database and MDX tree 
were not counted first. Fix: query the database and scan `src/content/articles/actualites/revue-*.mdx` before 
designing a retroactive migration. [Task 1]
  - Symptom: a gated page leaks the complete revue body. Cause: the server-side truncation boundary was bypassed or 
reimplemented incorrectly. Fix: preserve `<MobileOnly>` as the reliable split marker, fall back to first `## ` only 
when necessary, and verify the non-member response renders `RevuePaywall` without the full body. [Task 1]
  - Symptom: implementation begins before a source strategy is chosen. Cause: the 14 free MDX revues conflict with the 
intended gated flagship product. Fix: obtain an explicit A1/A2 decision and define the 14-day opening behavior before 
coding. [Task 2]


